        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(auto-reply): harden empty reply delivery",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFollow-up hardening for #100456 and #99712. A completed interactive turn must never disappear without a visible terminal reply, but progress notices, blank metadata, queued send policies, explicit silence, message-tool delivery, and pending continuations must not be mistaken for completion.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe first fix established the empty-reply fallback. Reading the full direct and queued delivery paths exposed nine coupled invariants that needed one canonical treatment:\n\n- distinguish visible output from committed outbound delivery;\n- keep queued delivery inside normal send-policy enforcement;\n- treat compaction notices as progress, not terminal replies;\n- carry fallback payloads through normal metadata, routing, and reply-to preparation;\n- reject whitespace-only and contentless payloads as visible output;\n- keep disabled reasoning/commentary lanes from consuming delivery bookkeeping;\n- preserve explicit silence, message-tool-only delivery, and pending continuations;\n- hold the queued reply lane until asynchronous recovery delivery settles; and\n- preserve group/channel silent-reply policy for the generated failure text.\n\nThe refactor removes the duplicate fallback helper and keeps failure copy plus conversation policy in the existing agent-runner execution owner.\n\n## User Impact\n\nInteractive direct and queued turns now either produce a genuinely visible response, complete a committed delivery, or emit the normal policy-aware failure reply. Hidden progress, blank payloads, suppressed lanes, or asynchronous dispatcher timing can no longer make a turn appear complete prematurely.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox exact-head focused matrix: 5 unit-fast tests, 456 auto-reply tests, and 86 end-to-end tests passed (547 total).\n- Blacksmith Testbox path-scoped `pnpm check:changed` covered all 14 touched files.\n- Fresh branch autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings (confidence 0.88).\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD` passed.\n\nRefs #100456\nRefs #99712\n",
